 dict(slug='cv-for-gulf-employers', title='What a Gulf employer looks for in a CV', cat='CV Tips', date='2026-11-13',
  excerpt='Recruiters in the UAE scan a CV in under a minute. Here is what they look for first and how to put it where they will see it.',
  keys=['Put your target role, phone, email and location at the very top.', 'Say clearly whether you can start now or need a visa.', 'List your latest job first, with short, specific duties.'],
  body=[('p','Recruiters in the UAE and wider GCC often scan a CV in well under a minute, especially when hundreds of people apply for one site or office job. Your goal is simple: make the answers to their first questions easy to find.'),
  ('h2','1. The top of the page decides everything'),
  ('p','Start with your **full name**, the **job you are applying for**, your **phone with WhatsApp**, **email** and **current location**. Under that, write a short professional summary of three or four lines: your trade, your years of experience, and the kind of site or company you want to work for.'),
  ('h2','2. Show your status and availability'),
  ('p','Employers in the Gulf need to know quickly if you can start immediately. Add your **nationality**, **visa status** and **availability** in one small line, for example: "Nationality: Kenyan | Visa: Employment visa | Available: Immediately".'),
  ('h2','3. Latest job first, with real duties'),
  ('p','List your most recent job first. For each job write the **job title, company, project or site, city and dates**. Under it use short bullet points that describe what you actually did, not a copy of the company brochure.'),
  ('ul',['Good: "Assisted pipe fitters with spool handling and flange alignment on a petrochemical project."','Weak: "Responsible for various duties as assigned."']),
  ('h2','4. Make your certificates easy to find'),
  ('p','Site safety certificates, licences and trade tests often decide who gets called. Keep them in their own section with the **name, issuer and year**, so a recruiter does not have to hunt for them.'),
  ('tip','Two pages is the sweet spot for most workers and technicians. One page is fine for beginners. Anything past three pages rarely gets read.'),
  ('h2','5. Keep it honest and consistent'),
  ('p','Dates, job titles and certificate names must match your documents. Employers in the region often verify, and a mismatch costs more than a short CV ever will.')]),

 dict(slug='what-is-ats', title='What is an ATS and how to get past it', cat='ATS', date='2026-11-12',
  excerpt='Many companies use software to read and sort CVs before a person sees them. Learn how it works and how to format your CV so it reads cleanly.',
  keys=['An ATS reads text, not design. Keep the layout simple.', 'Use standard headings like Experience, Education and Skills.', 'Use words from the job advert where they are true for you.'],
  body=[('p','An **ATS** (applicant tracking system) is software that many companies, recruiters and big contractors use to collect, read and rank CVs. If it cannot read your CV properly, a person may never see it.'),
  ('h2','How it reads your CV'),
  ('p','The software pulls out text and tries to sort it into fields: your name, contact details, job titles, employers, dates, skills and education. Fancy layouts break this process.'),
  ('h2','What breaks it'),
  ('ul',['Text boxes, tables and multiple complicated columns','Photos, logos and icons placed over the text','Headings with unusual names like "My Journey"','Information hidden in the header or footer of the file','Scanned images of a CV instead of real text']),
  ('h2','What helps it'),
  ('ol',['Use clear headings: Professional Summary, Experience, Education, Certificates, Skills.','Put job title, company and dates on the same line for each job.','Use a normal font such as Arial or Calibri.','Save as a PDF made from a document, or as a Word file, as the advert asks.','Use the exact words from the advert where they are true for you, for example the job title and the main tools or standards.']),
  ('tip','Our **ATS and Technical CV** is built exactly this way: plain layout, correct headings and keywords for your trade. A designed CV can still be used when a person reads it by hand.'),
  ('h2','Do not stuff keywords'),
  ('p','Adding words you cannot back up will not help. A human will read the CV after the software, and they will ask about everything on it.')]),

 dict(slug='job-performer-not-helper', title='Job performer, not helper: how to name your trade on your CV', cat='Site Jobs', date='2026-11-11',
  excerpt='On many Gulf projects the word is job performer, and the trade matters. Learn how to write Civil, Electrical or Scaffolding Job Performer correctly.',
  keys=['Write the trade first: Civil Job Performer, not just Helper.', 'The trade links you to the right safety training and tasks.', 'Use the same title on your CV, LinkedIn and certificates.'],
  body=[('p','On many large oil and gas and petrochemical projects, workers are described as **job performers** and the trade is part of the name. A plain "Helper" or "Job Performer" tells a recruiter very little. The trade tells them where you fit.'),
  ('h2','Why the trade matters'),
  ('p','Your job title decides which crew you join, which permits you work under and which safety training applies to you. For example: ADNOC WMS awareness, H2S awareness and permit-to-work briefings are all linked to the kind of work you do on site.'),
  ('h2','Examples of clear titles'),
  ('ul',['**Civil Job Performer**: excavation, concrete, formwork and rebar support','**Electrical Job Performer**: cable pulling, tray and conduit installation support','**Scaffolding Job Performer**: assisting with scaffold erection and dismantling','**Piping Job Performer**: pipe handling, fit-up support and flange work','**Mechanical Job Performer**: equipment installation and maintenance support','**Painting Job Performer**: surface preparation and coating support','**Insulation Job Performer**: insulation and cladding support']),
  ('h2','Add the company and the project'),
  ('p','Write the company and, if you can, the project too. For example: "Civil Job Performer | NSH | Project: Hail and Ghasha | Nov 2023 to date". The project name helps a recruiter place your experience immediately.'),
  ('tip','In our order form, choose your trade-specific role and fill in the optional Project box. We write the duties and skills to match.'),
  ('warn','Only use a title that matches what you really did and what is written in your documents. Do not upgrade "job performer" to "technician" or "foreman".')]),

 dict(slug='documents-before-you-apply', title='Documents to prepare before you apply for a Gulf job', cat='Visa and Documents', date='2026-11-10',
  excerpt='A clear folder of documents saves days when a recruiter asks for them. This is the checklist most workers and staff should have ready.',
  keys=['Keep clear scans, not dark phone photos.', 'Write your work history with exact employers and dates.', 'Name files clearly so they can be sent in seconds.'],
  body=[('p','Recruiters often ask for documents on the same day they call you. People who have everything ready in one folder get the next step first.'),
  ('h2','The basic checklist'),
  ('ul',['Passport copy: photo page and visa page if you have one','Recent passport-style photo with a plain background','Certificates, trade tests and licences','Experience or reference letters from past employers','Education certificates','Driving licence, if the job needs driving','Emirates ID or national ID copy, where you have it']),
  ('h2','How to scan well'),
  ('ol',['Use good light and place the document flat on a table.','Use a scanning app so the page is cropped straight and readable.','Check every name, number and date is sharp.','Save as PDF when a document has more than one page.']),
  ('h2','Name your files'),
  ('p','Use names like **Passport-Samuel-Otieno.pdf** and **H2S-Awareness-2025.pdf**, not "IMG_20261103.jpg". It saves the recruiter time and makes you look organised.'),
  ('h2','Write down your work history'),
  ('p','Before you start a CV, list each job: employer, project or site, city, job title, start and end month. Gaps are far easier to explain when the dates are accurate.'),
  ('tip','Our PDF tools can merge several scans into one PDF, rotate sideways pages and put them in order. They run on your phone, so your files stay with you.')]),

 dict(slug='site-safety-certificates', title='Safety certificates site employers often ask about', cat='Site Jobs', date='2026-11-09',
  excerpt='H2S awareness, working at height, confined space and more. What these certificates are and how to list them properly on your CV.',
  keys=['Requirements depend on the employer and the project.', 'List name, issuer and year for every certificate.', 'Keep the original certificates and scans safe and readable.'],
  body=[('p','Large industrial sites in the region often expect workers to hold basic safety training before they start. **Exact requirements depend on the employer, the client and the project**, so always confirm with the company. These are the certificates most commonly mentioned.'),
  ('h2','Common ones'),
  ('ul',['**H2S awareness**: hydrogen sulphide hazards and response','**ADNOC WMS or HSE induction**: for ADNOC-related work','**Basic safety induction**: site rules, PPE and emergency procedures','**Working at height**: fall prevention and safe access','**Confined space awareness**: entry hazards and permits','**Permit to work awareness**: how permits control risk','**First aid and CPR**, **fire fighting**, **banksman**, **rigger and slinger** for specific roles']),
  ('h2','How to list them on your CV'),
  ('p','Create a section called **Certificates and Licences**. For each one write the name, the training provider or issuer, and the year. Keep the newest at the top.'),
  ('h2','Keep them valid'),
  ('p','Many certificates expire. Note the expiry date in your own records and renew before it passes, so an employer never finds you holding an out-of-date card.'),
  ('warn','Never list a certificate you do not hold. Sites verify cards, and a false claim can cost you the job and future work.'),
  ('tip','We can lay out your certificates professionally and in the order you choose, in one clean file. See Other services.')]),

 dict(slug='cv-mistakes-gulf', title='10 CV mistakes that get Gulf applications rejected', cat='CV Tips', date='2026-11-08',
  excerpt='Small mistakes decide who gets called. Check your CV against this list before you send it again.',
  keys=['Most rejections come from simple, fixable mistakes.', 'Accuracy and clarity beat decoration.', 'Always proofread before sending.'],
  body=[('p','A CV rarely fails because of one big problem. It fails because of several small ones that tell a recruiter you are not careful. Check yours against this list.'),
  ('ol',['**No clear job title.** Say what you do: "Electrical Job Performer", not "Seeking opportunities".','**Missing contact details.** A phone number without WhatsApp, or a wrong email.','**No visa status or availability.** Employers must guess.','**Long paragraphs of duties.** Use short bullet points.','**Duties that are all the same for every job.** Be specific to each role.','**Dates that do not match your documents.**','**An unprofessional email address.** Use your name.','**Heavy design that breaks screening software.**','**Spelling mistakes**, especially in your own job title and company names.','**Too long.** More than three pages almost never gets read.']),
  ('tip','Ask a friend to read your CV for 30 seconds and tell you what job you want and where you work now. If they cannot, a recruiter will not be able to either.')]),

 dict(slug='visa-status-on-cv', title='How to show your visa status on a CV', cat='Visa and Documents', date='2026-11-07',
  excerpt='Honest, clear visa wording helps employers decide quickly. Here are simple ways to write it for each situation.',
  keys=['Always state your status. Do not leave it blank.', 'Be honest about dates, such as visit visa expiry or grace period.', 'Add when you can start.'],
  body=[('p','Employers in the Gulf need to know if they can hire you quickly. A clear visa line saves everyone time and builds trust.'),
  ('h2','Simple wording examples'),
  ('ul',['**Employment visa:** "Visa: Valid UAE employment visa | Available: Immediately"','**Visit visa:** "Visa: Visit visa, valid until 20 Dec 2026 | Available: Immediately"','**Cancelled visa:** "Visa: Cancelled, within grace period until 15 Dec 2026"','**Outside the UAE:** "Location: Nairobi, Kenya | Available: 2 weeks after job offer"']),
  ('h2','Why dates matter'),
  ('p','A visit visa or grace period has an end date. Including it shows you understand the timeline and lets the recruiter plan. Rules about grace periods and visa changes can change, so confirm current rules with your PRO, employer or the official immigration channels.'),
  ('warn','Never claim a visa status you do not have. Employers check, and false information can end an application at once.'),
  ('tip','Our order form asks for your visa status and expiry date, and places them neatly on your CV.')]),

